==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermissionGate  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_PermissionGate.als
    rationale: F_PermissionGate is the load-bearing constraint that ties op.succeeded to the (role,kind) matrix plus ownership. Removing it lets a non-owner non-admin member succeed at DeleteTask; the injection forces such an op into the universe, which LeastPrivilege/OwnershipBasedAccess are supposed to catch.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_008_OwnerOrAdminMayMutate, FR_009_MemberCannotMutateOthers
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_OwnerOrAdminMayMutate: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_MemberCannotMutateOthers: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CrossTeamIsolation  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_CrossTeamIsolation.als
    rationale: F_CrossTeamIsolation is what forbids a successful operation from reaching a task whose team differs from the caller's X-Team-Id. Clearing it allows cross-tenant access; the injection forces a successful GetTaskById whose target lives in a different team than teamCtx — exactly the leak NoInformationLeakage should flag. GetTaskById is used (not PATCH/DELETE) so no audit-task team chain re-enforces isolation.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_011_NoCrossTeamAccess, FR_014_CrossTeamIsolation
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_NoCrossTeamAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_CrossTeamIsolation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_StateChangingOpsProduceAudit  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_StateChangingOpsProduceAudit.als
    rationale: F_StateChangingOpsProduceAudit forces every successful POST/PATCH/DELETE to emit exactly one audit entry. Clearing it lets a mutation slip through unaudited; the injection forces a successful PostTasks with no producedAudit, which AuditCompleteness/FR-015 is supposed to catch.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_AuditPerSave
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditPerSave: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries says every audit row must be tied to exactly one originating operation — there are no orphans, no double-attribution. Removing it allows audit entries to appear without a producing op (i.e., 'injected' rows). The injection forces such an orphan, which AppendOnly should catch.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditAppendOnly, FR_018_AuditRetainedViaAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AuditRetainedViaAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: F_AuditAttribution binds the audit entry's actor and team to the operation's caller and teamCtx. Clearing it permits an audit row whose actor differs from the operation's caller — a misattribution. The injection forces such a mismatch, which AttributionCorrectness/FR-002 is supposed to catch.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_002_ActorFromAuthContext, FR_015_AuditPerSave
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_ActorFromAuthContext: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditPerSave: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_TaskOwnerIsTeamMember  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_TaskOwnerIsTeamMember.als
    rationale: F_TaskOwnerIsTeamMember anchors a task's owner to a real membership in the task's team. Removing it lets a task carry an owner who has no membership row. The injection forces such a task — exactly what OwnershipExclusivity/FR-006 is supposed to catch.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipExclusivity, FR_006_OwnerImmutableAndExclusive, FR_012_TaskFieldsValid
      - OwnershipExclusivity: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_OwnerImmutableAndExclusive: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_TaskFieldsValid: PASS (vacuous?)

